What is Git?

Answer:
Git is a Distributed Version Control System (DVCS) used to track changes in source code. It allows multiple developers to work on the same project and keeps a history of all changes.

2. What is GitHub?

Answer:
GitHub is a cloud-based platform that hosts Git repositories. It provides collaboration features such as Pull Requests, Issues, code reviews, and GitHub Actions.

3. What is the difference between Git and GitHub?
Git	GitHub
Version Control System	Repository Hosting Platform
Works locally	Works online
Tracks changes	Stores and shares repositories
Command-line tool	Web-based platform
What is an S3 Bucket

Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service) is an AWS service used to store and retrieve files over the internet.

A bucket is a container where files are stored in S3.

👉 In simple words:
S3 Bucket = Folder in the cloud used to store files.


What is Docker?

Docker is a containerization platform used to build, package, and run applications in containers.

Simple Definition

Docker is a tool that packages an application with all its dependencies into a container so it can run anywhere.
